        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Antonio Salieri, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n- Works: A Little Nightmare Music\n- Places: Legnago, Verona, Republic of Venice, Habsburg Monarchy\n- Roles: composer, conductor, teacher\n\nFacts:\n- Antonio Salieri was born on 18 August 1750 and died on 7 May 1825.\n- Antonio Salieri was an Italian classical composer, conductor, and teacher.\n- Antonio Salieri was born in Legnago, south of Verona, in the Republic of Venice.\n- Antonio Salieri spent his adult life and career as a subject of the Habsburg Monarchy.\n- A Little Nightmare Music is described as being based on a dream Antonio Salieri had on 4 December 1791, the night Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart died and Antonio Salieri did not.",
